<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Karak</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kerak, Kerak Castle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Karak is a town in central Jordan, east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dead-sea">Dead Sea</a>, dominated by Kerak Castle. The castle was begun in 1142 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/payen-the-butler">Payen the Butler</a> and became the centre of the crusader lordship of Oultrejordain, controlling routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. It fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s forces in 1188 after a long siege and remained a major stronghold under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubids</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-karak.jpg" alt="Al-Karak" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Teo Blancato · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:14_Al-Karak_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
